Build and run the SDL app with MSYS2 MINGW64:

    export PATH="/c/msys64/mingw64/bin:/c/msys64/usr/bin:$PATH"
    cmake -S . -B build -G "MinGW Makefiles"
    cmake --build build -j
    ./build/PatchKnob.exe

The SDL CMake target runs `sdlui/deploy_dlls.sh` after linking. That script
copies the transitive MSYS runtime DLLs next to `PatchKnob.exe`, so the build
folder can run without depending on whatever DLLs are elsewhere on PATH.
